<tr><td colspan=2>Dark eyes peer out from the shadows of the Wall of Blood.  Silently they watch the limping Death Knight approach with his heavy load.  A white haired Half-Elf.  Gouged in several places.  Just like the Death Knight.  Only a little bit more.  Normally, this would be a happy occasion.  Normally, she would be getting out her culinary tools and blood buckets.<br>
<br>
But not this night.  This was a special Half-Elf....even this morose Tier'Dal would admit that, though perhaps not in public.<br>
<br>
A large mass of living seawater stalks quietly by.  Totally in tune with its master, it feels her pain.  It reacts.  It rears up, preparing to rip the Death Knight to shreds.  "NO my pet" the Dark Mistress snarls quietly at her companion, "Let him live...it's not his fault...."  The fearsome beast lowers it daggers and continues to patrol the immediate area for anything that may bring harm.<br>
<br>
The Dark Mistress watches as the Death Knight pulls the cruel Dagger from his armor and places it in the fingers of the corpse.  She watches in silence still as he swears his final curse at her...and moves away, taken by the shadows.  She waits.  An hour passes before she is convinced she is truly alone.  She carefully creeps out to the body.  She touches the now stone cold flesh.  There is great grief, yet at the same time, her instincts tell her to be glad at this lightskin's passing.  Strangely - she sees a twisted logic in the two opposite emotions.<br>
<br>
Slowly she rises, swearing softly under her breath a curse to those that laid  this one low, as well as the dreadful little Gnome whose screams of agony have tormented her sleep the past few weeks.<br>
<br>
"What better way to mourn the loss of this one than to celebrate it?  I shall show all of Neriak what this was."  The Dark Mistress begins to soak the lightskin's blood up with the bits of torn cloth that cover the corpse.  She    runs through her hometown, splashing the now clotting mess on the walls, the taverns, and the bank as a salute to fallen heroes that she dared call friend.<br>
<br>
*******************************************************************************<br>
<br>
OOC - <br>
