<tr><td colspan=2>An Iksar watches silently the scene unfolding in Neriak, watches everyone having their own moments of thought at the pale corpse, even paler through the mist of the spirit world. She has been up there often, some would say too often.. It is the only place that will allow her any kind of rest, even with the risks involved. She recognizes the body, although she is more used to see it in another form.. "You always had it inside you, sister.. Your Hatred shone bright as the sun itself. There was no real need for the mask."<br>
The Iksar shakes her head.<br>
"But for those blind to the spirit world, it might have been necessary still."<br>
<br>
A sudden feeling reminds her that it is time. The sun is setting, she does not need to step down to see it, she knows already, within her soul.<br>
<br>
With a move she has done so often it has become second nature, the Iksar steps down into the physical world, and drops to her knees beside the bloodied corpse. She studies it for a moment, oblivious of the Teir'Dal strangers who are cringing away from her in fear. "<i>N'ai zhak'rah e, s'zch ci.. Srai 'kk ssra. N'oh..</i>" she whispers. The words echo faintly in the walls around the waterfall, a language which has never been heard within this city. "Rest well, sister.. May you never loose your way in the World of Dreams." With the last words, she picks up the Ragebringer, the last physical manifestation of her sister's Hatred.. and stabs it through her own chest, all the way up to the hilt.<br>
<br>
The Teir'Dal look at eachother in confusion, but feel their fear subsiding, although it still churns in their stomachs. Surely the creature is weak and ready for slaughter now. <br>
A few of them carefully step closer, weapons at the ready. <br>
<br>
Without opening her eyes she knows they are coming. She savours the pain for a moment still, a final memory of someone now lost to her. "How curious," she mutters through clenched teeth, "that something so pure as Hatred, can also be so truly inferior." She laughs at the strangers, whose Hatred spawned from Fear..<br>
In one motion, she pulls out the dagger from her scaled skin, and spins around, the point of the Ragebringer slashing open the ones who stood too close. The rest scream out in shock, and run for their lives, crashing into eachother, killing eachother to escape the scaled figure, who is still showing rows of sharp teeth in their direction, black eyes aflame with a frightening hate they could never have imagined from such an alien being.<br>
<br>
Silently she returns the dagger to the lifeless body before her. "You would have done this with style," she whispers, her last words to someone long gone. The Iksar steps back into the spirit world, leaving behind her a pale corpse, surrounded by a pool of dark blood, lifeless Teir'Dal littering the ground.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
